 "deviations_and_notes": [
  "IMPL-28 replaced the coordinator brief's slice-decrement residue scheme (which under-paid later rows) with full-pool shares and an end-of-allocate floor residue bounded by the open A count",
  "rows captured open but newly capped by this ticket are pruned when their real accounts are supplied, skipped with placeholders otherwise",
  "a discover that finds no open rows jumps to COMMIT (whole toll to seed); closed rows stay in the registry until a later ticket prunes them",
  "apply_senior/allocate_rows fold older pending into funded with watermark ticket.id − 1 (tickets are serial)",
  "the Book comparison checks liveness rather than registry slots because the Book drops capped rows immediately while the dense registry keeps them until prune",
  "the harness decodes U256 from the ticket bytes as two u128 limbs (no ethnum dependency)",
  "small claims are paid to a funded destination to avoid the runtime rent-exempt refusal",
  "ApplySenior.backer became optional after the harness showed the program-id placeholder failing Anchor's mut check"
